Here is a script that denies access to a website or service and responds with a custom error message:
```
<?php
 // Set the error message
 $error_message = "Access denied. You are not authorized to access this service.";

 // Set the HTTP status code
 $http_status_code = 403;

 // Set the content type
 $content_type = "text/plain";

 // Send the error message as a plain text response
 header("HTTP/1.1 ". $http_status_code. " Forbidden");
 header("Content-Type: ". $content_type);
 echo $error_message;
 exit;
?>
```
This script uses the `header()` function to set the HTTP status

